[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4026959428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4026959428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4026959428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wBoZE","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T21:15:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T21:15:25Z","body":"I'd say the persist is meant for nodes, don't think resource signals are saved, they're usually connected when assigned instead, as they are usually shared ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4026959428/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031316762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4031316762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4031316762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wSQMa","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T13:16:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T13:35:38Z","body":"I am working on a level editor where I use a resource to represent and save an undirected graph. This undirected graph stores a list of graph nodes, which are resources as well.\n\nIt is important for the level editor to be signaled that the undirected graph was modified. Hence I have a signal chain: graph node --> undirected graph --> level editor.\n\nThe graph node to undirected graph signal is a resource to resource signal. I can't create the connection  on `_ready` (does not exist) or on `_init` (the list of graph node is empty).\n\nTo save the resource to resource connections make sense because:\n- resource are used to save persistent data\n- resource don't have the luxury of a _ready function where we can recreate their connections","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031316762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031338804","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4031338804","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4031338804,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wSVk0","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T13:20:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T13:28:09Z","body":"I'm not sure about the exact situation here but I don't think the engine is designed to work this way, that's why signals in the engine code uses things like assignment to handle signals (like connecting `changed` of a texture when it is assigned)\n\nThis should be documented in that case, but I don't think this is by accident but rather by design\n\nEdit: Not sure but I think this is the part that handles connections specifically, and it checks specifically for node\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29b945f2eb52ef8d470f23649f584f4809ef5f39/scene/resources/packed_scene.cpp#L1167-L1174\n\nThe `PackedScene` code also works exclusively on nodes, and specifically expects that","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031338804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031505659","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4031505659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4031505659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wS-T7","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T13:47:03Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T13:47:03Z","body":"Yeah, that's a weird one. \n\nUsually, it is considered good practice to use resources when possible, but then it might be useful for saved resource to save their connections to their sub resources. I may write a proposal.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031505659/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031533479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4031533479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4031533479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wTFGn","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T13:51:22Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T13:51:22Z","body":"Using resources is absolutely appropriate, but their nature as shared objects make things a bit complex, *usually* resources have a clear relationship with what they are connected to, so there's usually no need to have a serialization of connections, as the connection would happen organically, but in cases where that doesn't apply it might be relevant, but I'm not sure what scope that would be and if it would be an appropriate use of resources","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4031533479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4037302014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4037302014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4037302014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wpFb-","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T08:10:17Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T08:10:17Z","body":"What do you mean by clear relationship?\n\nThe scope here is a resource that manages sub-resources and needs to listen to them (observer pattern). This situation can happen often, for instance: an inventory and its items, a graph and its nodes, etc. The sub-resources are added in editor, or in game. When we save and reload the resource, we still want it to listen to its sub-resources.\n\nIn a normal programming language, you would reconnect the objects on initialisation during the deserialisation. But here, it’s Godot that does it for us.\n\nI guess the bottom line is that I need to find a walk around for now ! 😄","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4037302014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4045573270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117264#issuecomment-4045573270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117264","id":4045573270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7xIoyW","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-12T10:21:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T10:25:41Z","body":"Here is the walkaround. First, let's note that the `_init` function in resources is called before the export variables are loaded, and the `NOTIFICATION_POSTINITIALIZE` does not seem to be called for resource. See similar report here:\nhttps://godotforums.org/d/30811-resource-initialization-troubles\n\nHence, the only solution is to use the setter of the sub-resource list:\n```gdscript\n@export var selected_objects:Array[A]=[]:\n    set(value):\n        selected_objects = value\n\t    for object in selected_objects:\n                object.transformed.connect(emit_transformed)\n```\nThis way when the resource is loading its sub-resource, we can automatically reconnect them.\n\nEDIT: Resource A also needs to have the `@tool` tag for this to work in editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4045573270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]